  "question": {
    "text": "If the formula of Borax is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>OH</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>&#183;</mo><msub><mi>zH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "17",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The crude name of borax is Tincal. It has the molecular formula&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo>.</mo><mn>10</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp;and structural formula of&nbsp;borax is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>OH</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p>Based on the structural formula,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>17</mn></math></p>",
